    "financial": {
      "valuation_insights": "### Valuation and Financial Highlights for Apple Inc. (Fiscal Year 2026)\n\nApple delivered record annual and quarterly financial performance, with total net sales reaching $478.83 billion, marking a 15.06% increase over FY 2025 [C:revenue_growth]. The operating income rose to $158.06 billion, yielding an operating margin of 33.01%, demonstrating efficient cost management on higher revenue [C:operating_margin]. Net income attributable to the company was $132.18 billion, accompanied by strong profitability with a GAAP diluted EPS of $8.98 [C:net_income][C:diluted_eps].\n\nThe company exhibited an outstanding return on average equity of 142.26%, reflecting robust profitability relative to shareholder investments [C:return_on_average_equity]. Leveraging was prudent with a debt-to-equity ratio including current portion at 0.70 times, indicating moderate financial risk [C:debt_to_equity]. Free cash flow was substantial at $136.06 billion, supporting ongoing investment and shareholder returns [C:free_cash_flow].\n\nApple's latest fiscal fourth quarter revenue was $114.48 billion, up 12% from the prior year’s same quarter, with a diluted EPS of $2.10 [C:latest_quarter_revenue][C:latest_quarter_eps]. The price-to-earnings ratio based on the October 30, 2026 stock price of $344.63 and FY 2026 diluted EPS is approximately 38.38 times, indicating market expectations for continued growth [C:price_to_earnings].\n\n**Peer Operating Margins Comparison:**\n- Microsoft Corp: 46.78% operating margin [C:peer_MSFT]\n- Alphabet Inc.: 32.03% operating margin [C:peer_GOOGL]\n- Oracle Corp: 30.59% operating margin [C:peer_ORCL]\n\nApple’s operating margin, while strong at 33.01%, trails Microsoft’s notably higher margin, suggesting potential for margin expansion or differing business model efficiencies.\n\nInsight: Apple's installed base of active devices reached a new all-time high across all platforms by the end of FY 2026, supporting its record revenue and EPS performance, as disclosed in the earnings release first paragraph [L000014].",
